# Sideways information passing (issue 809), every block holds a candidate: the athletes of the 1936 Summer games are spread over every block of the foaf:age scan (180,604 rows), so no block is skipped; the answer and the time must not be worse than without candidates.
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
PREFIX foaf: <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/>
PREFIX dbo: <http://dbpedia.org/ontology/>
PREFIX dbp: <http://dbpedia.org/property/>
PREFIX wso: <http://wallscope.co.uk/ontology/olympics/>
PREFIX wsr: <http://wallscope.co.uk/resource/olympics/>
SELECT ?a ?age WHERE { ?i wso:games <http://wallscope.co.uk/resource/olympics/games/1936/Summer> . ?i wso:athlete ?a . ?a foaf:age ?age }
